  "conclusions": [
    "C/D actual gain transistors59/60/111/112 and A/B slave hold71/72/87/88 are two distinct headroom targets. Original native source plan and adjacent physical resistor ownership are recorded, not inferred solely from names.",
    "Candidate control points for C/D are symmetric collector pullups182/183/220/221 and shunts184/185/222/223, upstream follower loads187/188/225/226, or owned input conductors. Their direction cannot be selected safely from transistor extrema without separating same-row conductor drop, follower headroom and collector load currents.",
    "Candidate control points for A/B are slave emitter bleeds198/210 and output loads191/194/202/205. A stronger bleed or changed load can alter regeneration, dynamic current and downstream loading; no numeric resistor change follows from a required VCE difference alone.",
    "C/D negative margin at0.3UI becomes positive at0.6UI in nominal cases; the observed failure does not justify a polarity swap or clock pin swap.",
    "Zero first-latch collector-voltage difference crossings do not establish failed current steering. Compare actual sums of the two parallel cp and two parallel cn collector currents on each shared tail, retaining distinct native nodes, rather than imposing a zero-voltage crossing requirement.",
    "Original captured selected188-column caches include all32 clock HBT currents and all8 failed HBT C/B/E/current traces. They do not include all adjacent resistor terminal voltages and upstream follower C/B/E/current, so they cannot alone close a complete same-row KCL ledger. Any next capture readback should batch all required nodes/branches once, authenticate the original full capture and reproduce the unchanged rejection first."
